========================================================================
[d] PROOF-ATTEMPT structural facts
========================================================================
  Fact 1 (H=H^op): the maximizer SET is closed under rho (converse-relabel),
    because H(T)=H(T^op) always (reverse a Ham path -> Ham path of T^op),
    and rho realizes the converse-relabel as a coordinate involution (THM-280).
    => the set of maximizing tilings is a UNION of rho-orbits.
  Fact 2 (needed): HYP-2688 needs >=1 rho-FIXED maximizer (a grid-sym tiling).
    A rho-orbit of size 2 (a non-grid-sym tiling + its mirror) does NOT by
    itself give a fixed point. So Fact 1 alone is INSUFFICIENT.
    Verdict per n (does some grid-sym tiling attain the global max?):
      n=5: grid-sym attains global max = True
      n=6: grid-sym attains global max = True
      n=7: grid-sym attains global max = True
      n=8: grid-sym attains global max = True
      n=9: grid-sym attains global max = True

